        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "{\"output\":\"# Service component\\n\\nFix transfer(connection, publisher, source, target, amount) in src/service.py. A successful transfer debits and credits exactly once, appends one ledger row, commits, then publishes {'source': source, 'target': target, 'amount': amount}. source and target must differ and exist; amount is a positive integer, excluding bool, and cannot exceed the source balance. Invalid transfers raise ValueError without writes or publication. Database failure at any statement or commit rolls back all changes and never publishes. Publication failure propagates after the committed transfer and must not undo it. Caller connections are idle at entry. Keep balance reads and account setup intact. Start in src/service.py and src/repository.py.\\n\\nRun `python3 checks/public.py` from the project root. Implementation belongs in src/. Add checks under checks/.\\nfrom .repository import move\\n\\ndef transfer(connection, publisher, source, target, amount):\\n    publisher.publish({\\\"source\\\": source, \\\"target\\\": target, \\\"amount\\\": amount})\\n    move(connection, source, target, amount)\\n    connection.commit()\\ndef initialize(connection):\\n    connection.executescript(\\\"CREATE TABLE accounts(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, balance INTEGER NOT NULL); CREATE TABLE ledger(source TEXT, target TEXT, amount INTEGER);\\\")\\n    connection.commit()\\n\\ndef balance(connection, account):\\n    row = connection.execute(\\\"SELECT balance FROM accounts WHERE id=?\\\", (account,)).fetchone()\\n    return None if row is None else row[0]\\n\\ndef move(connection, source, target, amount):\\n    connection.execute(\\\"UPDATE accounts SET balance=balance-? WHERE id=?\\\", (amount, source))\\n    connection.execute(\\\"UPDATE accounts SET balance=balance+? WHERE id=?\\\", (amount, target))\\n    connection.execute(\\\"INSERT INTO ledger VALUES (?, ?, ?)\\\", (source, target, amount))\\nclass Recorder:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.events = []\\n\\n    def publish(self, event):\\n        self.events.append(event.copy())\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"signal\":null,\"cancelled\":false,\"timeout\":false,\"truncated\":false}"
          }
